    "result": "Perfect! All the requirements have been successfully implemented:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\n### 1. **Added `renderSummary()` function** (`src/gate/report.ts`)\n   - Exports a new function that formats gate results as a one-line summary\n   - Format: `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>`\n   - Appends blocked check IDs in GATE_CHECKS order when there are blocks\n   - Special case: returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure` when gate section is missing\n   - Correctly counts answered checks (those without block-severity findings; warnings don't reduce count)\n\n### 2. **Added `--summary` flag to CLI** (`src/cli.ts`)\n   - Integrated into the `check` command\n   - Outputs only the summary line instead of full report\n   - `--json` flag has priority when both are specified\n   - Exit codes unchanged (1 on BLOCK, 0 otherwise)\n   - Updated HELP text to document the new flag\n\n### 3. **Added comprehensive tests** (`src/gate/report.test.ts`)\n   - 7 new test cases covering:\n     - Missing gate section case\n     - All checks passing\n     - Only warnings (no blocks)\n     - Blocked checks with proper formatting\n     - Duplicate findings for same check\n     - Out-of-order findings\n     - Mixed warnings and blocks\n\n### 4. **Exported function** (`src/index.ts`)\n   - Added `renderSummary` to module exports\n\n### Verification \u2713\n- \u2705 Build succeeds with `pnpm --filter frai-gate build`\n- \u2705 All 18 tests pass (7 new + 11 existing)\n- \u2705 CLI help text updated\n- \u2705 Exit codes correct (0 for PASS/WARN, 1 for BLOCK)\n- \u2705 Flag priority respected (--json > --summary)\n- \u2705 Format matches specification with examples\n\nThe feature is ready for use and provides concise one-line summaries perfect for CI logs.",
